WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:04.460 --> 00:00:07.560
We've been waiting for this car for a long
time.

00:00:07.560 --> 00:00:11.200
We're in Opel's central plant in Rüsselsheim.

00:00:11.200 --> 00:00:13.090
Hallo!

00:00:13.090 --> 00:00:14.980
Hallo.

00:00:14.980 --> 00:00:20.640
So that's it, the Opel Ampera E. Made in the
USA

00:00:20.640 --> 00:00:21.670
That's not exactly true.

00:00:21.670 --> 00:00:25.349
It was developed in cooperation with our colleagues
at Chevrolet.

00:00:25.349 --> 00:00:26.460
We were equal partners.

00:00:26.460 --> 00:00:32.400
There's plenty of Opel DNA in there, as you'll
see for yourself!

00:00:32.400 --> 00:00:35.940
The car has been touted as Opel's hope for
the future.

00:00:35.940 --> 00:00:39.440
It's fully electric with state-of-the-art
battery technology.

00:00:39.440 --> 00:00:45.399
But where's it being made, exactly?

00:00:45.399 --> 00:00:48.100
It's being assembled in Orion, Michigan, in
the US.

00:00:48.100 --> 00:00:50.480
Sure, it's an import.

00:00:50.480 --> 00:00:53.530
The car is only made on their production line.

00:00:53.530 --> 00:00:55.310
So it's not made in Rüsselsheim.

00:00:55.310 --> 00:00:57.179
That's right

00:00:57.179 --> 00:00:58.949
May I get in?

00:00:58.949 --> 00:01:01.609
Of course.

00:01:01.609 --> 00:01:07.280
Parent company General Motors is making and
selling this model in the US as the Chevrolet

00:01:07.280 --> 00:01:08.320
Bolt.

00:01:08.320 --> 00:01:13.350
In Europe it's being brought to market as
the Ampera E. Supply is extremely limited

00:01:13.350 --> 00:01:16.780
because GM is selling off its Opel unit.

00:01:16.780 --> 00:01:19.950
The future of this electric model is unclear.

00:01:19.950 --> 00:01:29.450
We've been told we're the first German TV
team to test the vehicle.

00:01:29.450 --> 00:01:36.630
We're driving from Rüsselsheim to Bergisch-Gladbach,
a distance of 180 kilometres.

00:01:36.630 --> 00:01:43.040
We're going to meet the car expert who can
explain why this car took so long to deliver.

00:01:43.040 --> 00:01:47.579
When it finally comes to market, it will be
the longest-range e-car in Germany -- up to

00:01:47.579 --> 00:01:52.170
500 kilometres range.

00:01:52.170 --> 00:02:06.590
And I'm about to take it out onto the Autobahn,
where we'll see how far it really can drive.

00:02:06.590 --> 00:02:09.479
The car is full of lights and bells and whistles.

00:02:09.479 --> 00:02:16.070
It encourages the driver to drive more slowly,
drive more economically.

00:02:16.070 --> 00:02:22.340
Or like right now for example, generate energy
while driving down hills.

00:02:22.340 --> 00:02:24.780
It's an entirely new way of driving.

00:02:24.780 --> 00:02:29.260
The only problem is, we have that appointment
coming up and I have to hurry a bit to get

00:02:29.260 --> 00:02:41.690
there on time.

00:02:41.690 --> 00:02:52.670
We want to know what will happen to the Ampera
E when French corporation PSA takes over Opel.

00:02:52.670 --> 00:02:57.650
Of course it's clear to GM that electromobility
is the technology of the future, so GM wanted

00:02:57.650 --> 00:03:00.670
to maintain it as a core competency.

00:03:00.670 --> 00:03:05.900
So the entire competency was brought to the
US, to Detroit, including all patents and

00:03:05.900 --> 00:03:08.340
everything else that's connected with it.

00:03:08.340 --> 00:03:15.460
You can expect something similar between PSA
and Opel.

00:03:15.460 --> 00:03:20.860
The core competencies of electromobility will
be held in Paris rather than Rüsselsheim.

00:03:20.860 --> 00:03:25.750
That's too bad.

00:03:25.750 --> 00:03:30.050
Well, it's something we have to live with.

00:03:30.050 --> 00:03:35.630
I think Opel first has to show that it can
make money and further improve its image.

00:03:35.630 --> 00:03:40.860
An Opel Ampera E could help with that.

00:03:40.860 --> 00:03:48.490
Though that won't happen if GM is barely shipping
any cars to Europe."

00:03:48.490 --> 00:03:52.700
In Norway are there are already 4000 orders
for the car.

00:03:52.700 --> 00:03:55.720
That's due to the car's unusually long range.

00:03:55.720 --> 00:03:59.480
But there's a waiting list of up to one and
a half years.

00:03:59.480 --> 00:04:01.330
That looks like a charging station.

00:04:01.330 --> 00:04:06.480
I'm going to drive in there now.

00:04:06.480 --> 00:04:21.980
I hope it works.

00:04:21.980 --> 00:04:25.909
It's working!

00:04:25.909 --> 00:04:29.740
Success!

00:04:29.740 --> 00:04:34.690
So, have a look.

00:04:34.690 --> 00:04:36.780
310 kilometre range.

00:04:36.780 --> 00:04:40.610
We've reached that after charging for half
an hour.

00:04:40.610 --> 00:04:42.039
This is a good car.

00:04:42.039 --> 00:04:46.439
It's comfortable and it runs well.

00:04:46.439 --> 00:04:50.440
You can reserve an Ampera E for a fee of 1000
euros.

00:04:50.440 --> 00:04:54.270
But Opel gives you no guarantee that you'll
actually get one.

